hange, ship/doctor-final.json = AFTER), AGENTS.md, pipeline/lib/gate.mjs, pipeline/lib/git.mjs, src/repo.ts, src/community/weekly-run-report/v1/*, the m0saic CLI source at C:\\\\src\\\\m0saic\\\\packages\\\\cli\\\\src\\\\templateDoctor.ts, the 0.3.1 types at C:\\\\src\\\\m0saic\\\\packages\\\\types\\\\src\\\\template-repo\\\\template-repo.ts, the 0.3.1 knowledge base at C:\\\\src\\\\m0saic\\\\packages\\\\knowledge\\\\docs\\\\.\nReport each finding with: claim (what you checked), verdict (true|false|unverifiable), severity (blocker = gate would fail or a hard rule broken; fix-text = a sentence in the journal/WHY is wrong and should be reworded; note = minor), evidence (file:line, command output, numbers), suggestedFix. Also include findings you CONFIRMED true (verdict true, severity note) so the caller sees coverage.`\n\nconst SCHEMA = {\n  type: 'object',\n  properties: {\n    lens: { type: 'string' },\n    summary: { type: 'string' },\n    findings: {\n      type: 'array',\n      items: {\n        type: 'object',\n        properties: {\n          claim: { type: 'string' },\n          verdict: { type: 'string', enum: ['true', 'false', 'unverifiable'] },\n          severity: { type: 'string', enum: ['blocker', 'fix-text', 'note'] },\n          evidence: { type: 'string' },\n          suggestedFix: { type: 'string' },\n        },\n        required: ['claim', 'verdict', 'severity', 'evidence'],\n      },\n    },\n  },\n  required: ['lens', 'summary', 'findings'],\n}\n\nconst LENSES = [\n  {\n    key: 'repo-conventions',\n    prompt: `LENS: the repo.conventions change. The ship agent found that 'm0saic doctor . --json' (CLI 0.3.2, a symlink to C:\\\\src\\\\m0saic\\\\packages\\\\cli) reported ok:false with one error: catalogSidecar (a 0.3.1 rule) on today's new template. It responded by adding conventions: \"0.3.0\" to TEMPLATE_REPO in src/repo.ts (with an intersection type because the repo's node_modules @m0saic/types is 0.2.0). Try to refute that this was correct and safe:\n1. Read templateDoctor.ts: confirm how repo.conventions is read (from the loaded repo export), how heldToFor/effectiveConventionLine treat a template with no shipped line, and that with target 0.3.0 the new template is still held to EVERY rule up to 0.3.0 (i.e. only rules newer than 0.3.0 become lag). List exactly which conventions are newer than 0.3.0 (TEMPLATE_CONVENTION_SINCE in C:\\\\src\\\\m0saic\\\\packages\\\\template-utils\\\\src\\\\template\\\\templateConventions.ts or wherever it lives) — does the target hide anything other than catalogSidecar for today's template? Compare journal/2026-10-06/scratch/ship-doctor.json (before) vs journal/2026-10-06/scratch/ship/doctor-final.json (after): did today's template have ANY finding other than catalogSidecar before? Any change in how OLD templates are judged (errors that became lag or vice versa)?\n2. Is \"0.3.0\" the truthful target? Check frozen.manifest.json release, the repo's package.json @m0saic deps, whether tools/ (read only) has any catalog/sidecar gathering step (grep tools/ and src/gen-template-manifest.ts for 'catalog').\n3. Scope: per pipeline/lib/git.mjs classifyChanges, is a change to src/repo.ts allowed for a day? Is src/repo.ts in frozen.manifest.json 'files'? Does AGENTS.md forbid it anywhere?\n4. Safety: template-manifest.json now carries repo.conventions. Does tools/contract-check.mjs or any loader validate repo keys strictly? Does the 0.3.x loader in the CLI (C:\\\\src\\\\m0saic\\\\packages\\\\*) do anything else with repo.conventions (grep for 'conventions' under packages/*/src for repo-level reads) that could change runtime behaviour or rendering?\n5. Is it the documented mechanism? Quote the doc lines (knowledge docs cli-usage.md / standalone-pack-authoring.md) and the founder line about NEW templates meeting the CURRENT line — weigh it honestly: does targeting 0.3.0 contradict the docs' intent for a repo like this one?\nYou may run 'm0saic doctor . --json' (read-only) and node one-liners that only read.`,\n  },\n  {\n    key: 'ship-doc-truth',\n    prompt: `LENS: every factual claim in journal/2026-10-06/50-ship.md. Go sentence by sentence. Check against the files: the critique scores (15/18 etc. — note the critique's score table has 9 columns; is \"15/18\" a correct way to write a's score? check the rubric max in 20-brief.md), the timeline sums ($70.01, 7 phase calls) via 'node pipeline/lib/trace.mjs --timeline journal/2026-10-06/trace.json', test counts (368 jest, 61 node — see journal/2026-10-06/scratch/ship-chain-final.log), preview size (assets/templates/@one-a-day__community__weekly-run-report__v1/preview.png), every relative link resolves to an existing file (links are relative to journal/2026-10-06/), the 0.3.2 release time claim (git -C C:\\\\src\\\\m0saic log -5 --date=iso — read-only), the quoted doc sentence exists in C:\\\\src\\\\m0saic\\\\packages\\\\knowledge\\\\docs\\\\runtime\\\\cli-usage.md, the official repos' conventions claim (C:\\\\src\\\\m0saic\\\\packages\\\\templates\\\\src\\\\repo.ts and community-templates). Weak spots: verify each against 40-critique.md and the images. In particular VERIFY THE FAINT BLOCK CLAIM: crop and upscale (ffmpeg is on PATH or under ~/m0saic; e.g. ffmpeg -i in.png -vf \"crop=w:h:x:y,scale=iw*6:ih*6:flags=neighbor\" out.png) the area right of the '214' in journal/2026-10-06/scratch/ship/story-empty.png (around x 440-500, y 500-560) and right of '187' in journal/2026-10-06/scratch/ship/week-313.png (around x 395-440, y 320-370), write crops under journal/2026-10-06/scratch/verify-ship/, Read them, and say whether a lighter block is really there and roughly its size in px. Also try to get pixel values (ffmpeg -f rawvideo or a crop to .ppm/.pgm then read bytes with node) to state the tile level vs block level. Also check the render commands: run each 'Props worth trying' line as m0saic make ... --validate-only -o journal/2026-10-06/scratch/verify-ship/<name>.png and report exit codes (in bash, single-quoted JSON works as written).`,\n  },\n  {\n    key: 'why-truth',\n    prompt: `LENS: the template's WHY block and header in src/community/weekly-run-report/v1/weekly-run-report.ts. (a) The WHY.timeline must be VERBATIM the output of 'node pipeline/lib/trace.mjs --timeline journal/2026-10-06/trace.json' — parse both and deep-compare; report any difference. (b) The WHY.solution, caveats, usage.try and the header comment must describe variant a (two big hero tiles for finishers and volunteers over four smaller stat tiles; milestone band always present; 6-10 clubs in two rows) — not variant b (six equal tiles) or c (night page). Compare with journal/2026-10-06/variants/b/src and c/src to make sure no b/c wording leaked into a. (c) Every claim in WHY that can be checked against the code: e.g. 'numbers capped at 1/1.6 of the headline size', 'No parkrun name, logo or colours' (grep the defaults and labels for 'parkrun' — the user's own eventName may contain it, defaults must not), the V prefix, 'On a thumbnail such as 480x270, seven or more clubs may be refused' (you may test with m0saic make ... -w 480 -h 270 --props '{\"milestones\":\"1xR25, 1xR50, 1xR100, 1xR250, 1xR500, 1xV25, 1xV50\"}' --validate-only -o journal/2026-10-06/scratch/verify-ship/thumb7.png), the usage.command syntax (--props @week.json), the quotes in WHY.problem appear in journal/2026-10-06/10-scout.md or scout-notes. (d) ASCII only in all WHY strings. (e) WHY.model equals journal/2026-10-06/run.json model.selfDeclared and WHY.day equals run.json day. Run 'node tools/check-why.mjs --json' (read-only) and report its result.`,\n  },\n  {\n    key: 'gate-dry-run',\n    prompt: `LENS: would the runner's gate (pipeline/lib/gate.mjs) pass right now? Simulate it READ-ONLY. Write a small node ESM script UNDER journal/2026-10-06/scratch/verify-ship/ that imports ONLY { classifyChanges, porcelain } from the repo's pipeline/lib/git.mjs (by absolute file URL) and prints classifyChanges(porcelain(REPO), { date: '2026-10-06' }) — DO NOT import or call revertPaths, commitAll, push, snapshotTree or runGate. Check: forbidden is empty; scratch list (what would be deleted) contains nothing that matters; exactly one newTemplateDirs entry 'src/community/weekly-run-report/v1/'; touchedAssetDirs is exactly ['@one-a-day__community__weekly-run-report__v1']; template-manifest.json has repo.repoId and an entry for the template; preview.png >= 5 KB; journal/2026-10-06/50-ship.md exists; state.json has decision 'ship' and pick 'a'. Then run read-only the gate's checks that do not mutate: 'node tools/check-freeze.mjs' (WITHOUT --update), 'm0saic doctor . --json' (parse ok), 'm0saic make @one-a-day/community/weekly-run-report/v1 --template-repo . --validate-only --quiet' and the same with --tutorial (these write nothing without -o --report; if unsure add -o journal/2026-10-06/scratch/verify-ship/x.png). Also check: no stray out.*/why.*/*.validate.json/*.output.json at the repo root; no files changed under other days' journal folders; dist/ is in sync with src (e.g. dist/repo.js contains conventions \"0.3.0\"; dist/community/weekly-run-report/v1/weekly-run-report.js contains the 7-phase timeline incl. 'critique (2)'); git diff --stat (read-only) of tracked files looks like only wiring + generated files + src/repo.ts. Also confirm nothing under src/<pack>/<slug>/vN that exists at HEAD was modified (git diff --name-only HEAD -- src). Report every check as a finding.`,\n  },\n]\n\nphase('Verify')\nconst results = await parallel(LENSES.map(l => () =>\n  agent(`${COMMON}\\n\\n${l.prompt}`, { label: `verify:${l.key}`, phase: 'Verify', schema: SCHEMA })\n))\nconst ok = results.filter(Boolean)\nlog(`${ok.length}/${LENSES.length} lenses returned`)\nconst flagged = ok.flatMap(r => r.findings.filter(f => f.verdict !== 'true' || f.severity !== 'note').map(f => ({ lens: r.lens, ...f })))\nreturn { summaries: ok.map(r => ({ lens: r.lens, summary: r.summary })), flagged, all: ok }\n","uuid":"e3c3e39d-7e2a-4da3-b534-0ad21faa9764","session_id":"7dfecaa2-57f9-440a-a400-57b554bd1f45"}
